@242 = ~Free Action (Abjuration)
Level: 4
Sphere: charm
Range: touch
Duration: 1 turn + 1 round/level
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: creature touched
Saving Throw: none

While under the effects of this spell, the recipient becomes immune to anything that limits his movement. This includes the effects of web, hold person, grease and entangle. Having lost all healing abilities, the Preacher of Flames casts a version of this spell that cannot free a creature already paralyzed.~
@2421 = ~Free Action (Abjuration)
Level: 4
Sphere: charm
Range: touch
Duration: 1 turn / level
Casting Time: 7
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: none

This spell gives the affected creature an immunity to magic that impedes movement (such as Grease, Web, or Slow spells) and protects against paralysis, hold and stun effects. The recipient of the spell can still be hasted and receive beneficial movement effects such as those granted by the boots of speed.
Special: Having lost all healing abilities, the Preacher of Flames casts a version of this spell that cannot free a creature already paralyzed.~ //Texte pour IWDEE

@246 = ~Animal Summoning I (Conjuration, Summoning)
Level: 4
Sphere: animal, conjuration
Range: 20 m
Duration: 3 turns
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: special
Saving Throw: none

By means of this spell, the caster calls up to three animals that have 4 Hit Dice or less. Fire creatures and creatures with an affinity for fire answer the Fire Lord's call in place of the animals normally summoned. They will remain under the caster's control until slain or the spell duration expires.~
@2461 = ~Firedrake~
@2462 = ~Fire Spider~
@2463 = ~Firenewt~

@247 = ~Conjure Lesser Fire Elemental~
@248 = ~Conjure Lesser Fire Elemental (Conjuration, Summoning)
Level: 4
Sphere: elemental (fire)
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 1 turn + 1 round / level
Casting Time: 1 round
Area of Effect: special
Saving Throw: none

This spell allows the cleric to summon lesser fire elementals. The elementals will do everything in their power to help the preacher as long as the spell lasts, after which they will return to their plane of existence.
The number and strength of the elementals depend on where the portal opens on their plane. Each casting has a 50% chance to summon 1 to 4 elementals with 2 Hit Dice, a 30% chance to summon 1 to 3 with 4 Hit Dice, and a 20% chance to summon 1 or 2 with 6 Hit Dice.~
@2481 = ~Lesser Fire Elemental~

@249 = ~Ignition~
@2410 = ~Ignition (Necromancy)
Level: 4
Sphere: necromancy
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 5 rounds
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: negates

If the target of the spell fails a save vs. spell, it catches fire. For the next 5 rounds during which the flames burn his flesh, the victim suffers the following damage: 4D10 +5, 4D8 +4, 4D6 +3, 4D4 +2, 4D2 +1, after which the flames die out. When it catches fire, the victim must make another save vs. spell or flee in terror of burning alive.
The spell burns flesh and boils blood. The resulting agony imposes a -2 penalty to all rolls, including attack rolls, for 9 rounds. The pain persists after the flames die out.
Fire creatures are immune to Ignition.~
@24101 = ~Ignition (Necromancy)
Level: 4
Sphere: necromancy
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 5 rounds
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: negates

If the target of the spell fails a save vs. spell, it catches fire. For the next 5 rounds while flames burn his flesh, the victim suffers the following damage: 4D10 +10, 4D8 +8, 4D6 +6, 4D4 +4, 4D2 +2, after which the flames die out. When it catches fire, the victim must make another save vs. spell or flee in terror of burning alive.
The spell burns flesh and boils blood. The resulting agony imposes a -2 penalty to all rolls, including attack rolls, for 9 rounds. The pain persists after the flames die out.
At caster level 30, the damage becomes 3D12 +12, 3D10 +10, 3D8 +8, 3D6 +6, 3D4 +4.
At caster level 40, the flames burn for a sixth round, dealing 4D12 +6, 4D10 +5, 4D8 +4, 4D6 +3, 4D4 +2, 4D2 +1.
Fire creatures are immune to Ignition.~
@24102 = ~Ignition (Necromancy)
Level: 4
Sphere: necromancy
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 5 rounds
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: negates

If the target of the spell fails a save vs. spell at a -2 penalty (an additional -1 for every 5 levels of the caster beyond level 20), it catches fire. For the next 5 rounds during which the flames burn his flesh, the victim suffers the following damage: 4D10 +5, 4D8 +4, 4D6 +3, 4D4 +2, 4D2 +1, after which the flames die out. When it catches fire, the victim must make another save vs. spell or flee in terror of burning alive.
The spell burns flesh and boils blood. The resulting agony imposes a -2 penalty to all rolls, including attack rolls, for 9 rounds. The pain persists after the flames die out.
Fire creatures are immune to Ignition.~

@2411 = ~Fire Form~
@2412 = ~Fire Form (Transmutation)
Level: 4
Sphere: elemental (fire)
Range: 0
Duration: 1 turn + 1 round / level
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

When he casts this spell, the body of the preacher of flames gradually turns into fire, while his equipment blends into the mass to adopt the final shape of a fire elemental. In this form, he becomes immune to all types of fire damage, as well as poisons, non-magical weapons and backstabs. His natural armor class is set at 4 and his fists inflict additional 1D8 fire damage. His THAC0, ability scores and hit points stay the same, and he keeps the ability to cast spells. While in elemental form, he burns web, entangling roots and grease, safely passing through each of these.~
@24121 = ~Fire Form (Transmutation)
Level: 4
Sphere: elemental (fire)
Range: 0
Duration: 3 turns
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

When he casts this spell, the body of the preacher of flames gradually turns into fire, while his equipment blends into the mass to adopt the final shape of a fire elemental. In this form, he becomes immune to all types of fire damage, as well as poisons, non-magical weapons and backstabs. His natural armor class is set at 4 and his fists inflict additional 1D10 (2D6 -1 at level 30 and 1D12 at level 40) fire damage. His THAC0, ability scores and hit points stay the same, and he keeps the ability to cast spells. While in elemental form, he burns web, entangling roots and grease, safely passing through each of these.~

@2413 = ~Fire Breath~
@2414 = ~Fire Breath (Alteration)
Level: 4
Sphere: elemental (fire)
Range: 5 meters
Duration: instantaneous
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: 80-degree arc
Saving Throw: half

The preacher breathes a cone of fire up to 4 meters long, dealing 1D4 + 2 points of fire damage per level to all creatures caught in the cone (maximum 12D4 + 24). Creatures that successfully save vs. breath weapon suffer only half damage.

~
@24141 = ~Fire Breath (Alteration)
Level: 4
Sphere: elemental (fire)
Range: 5 meters
Duration: instantaneous
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: 80-degree arc
Saving Throw: half

The preacher breathes a cone of fire up to 4 meters long, dealing 15D4 + 27 points of fire damage to all creatures caught in the cone (16D4 + 30 at level 30 and 17D4 + 33 at level 40). Creatures that successfully save vs. breath weapon suffer only half damage.

~
@24142 = ~Fire Breath (Alteration)
Level: 4
Sphere: elemental (fire)
Range: 5 meters
Duration: instantaneous
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: 80-degree arc
Saving Throw: half

The preacher breathes a cone of fire up to 4 meters long, dealing 12D4 + 24 points of fire damage to all creatures caught in the cone. Creatures that successfully save vs. breath weapon at -2 (an additional -1 for every 5 levels of the spellcaster beyond level 20) suffer only half damage.

~

@2415 = ~Lower Fire Resistance II~
@2416 = ~Lower Fire Resistance II (Abjuration, Alteration)
Level: 4
Sphere: charm, elemental (fire)
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 5 rounds + 1 round / level
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: 10-meter radius
Saving Throw: half

When the preacher of flames casts this spell, elemental energies sweep through the chosen area. All creatures present in the area must make a successful save vs. spell or have their fire resistance reduced by 3% per level of the preacher (max 60%). Magic resistance offers no protection. A successful save halves the reduction in fire resistance.~

